{number: 143}
{title: Under His Wings}
{key: C}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[C] Under His wings I am safely a-[F] biding,
Though the night [C] deepens and tempests are [G7] wild,
Still [C] I can trust Him; I know He will [F] keep me,
He has re-[C] deemed me, and [G7] I am His [C] child.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
Under His [F] wings, under His [C] wings,
Who from His [G7] love can sever?
Under His [C] wings my soul shall a-[F] bide,
Safely a-[C] bide for-[G7] ever. [C]
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 2}
[C] Under His wings, what a refuge in [F] sorrow!
How the heart [C] yearns for the blessing of [G7] rest!
Unto [C] the cross I have fled for pro-[F] tection,
Pardon and [C] peace I have [G7] found in His [C] breast.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
[C] Under His wings, oh, what precious en-[F] joyment!
There will I [C] hide till life's trials are [G7] o'er;
Sheltered, [C] protected, no evil can [F] harm me,
Resting in [C] Jesus for-[G7] ever-[C] more.
{end_of_verse}
